+# Production Certification Checklist & Scripts
+
+This document lists the final steps and scripts to use for production certification; run these with your security and SRE teams.
+
+1) PCR policy signing and deploy
+ - Security team composes PCR policy JSON at services/attestation_verifier/attestation_policy.json
+ - Use services/attestation_verifier/pcr_policy_sign.py to sign with private key (or use KMS signing)
+ - Upload signed policy to cluster secret (signed_policy.json) and public key to POLICY_PUB_PATH
+ - Restart attestation-verifier to pick up signed policy
+
+2) Cosign KMS signing
+ - Configure COSIGN_AWS_KMS_KEY_ARN or equivalent in CI secrets
+ - Use .github/workflows/cosign_kms_sign.yml to build & sign images
+ - Install Kyverno policy require-signed-images-in-production in cluster
+
+3) Safety calibration
+ - Provide labeled safety calibration file (JSONL) to CI (SAFETY_CALIB_DATA)
+ - Run .github/workflows/safety_calibrate_and_gate.yml (calibration will produce thresholds.json)
+ - Deploy resulting thresholds.json to /etc/safety/thresholds.json in safety-detectors service via configmap/secret
+
+4) OIDC & TLS
+ - Populate rater-oauth-secrets Kubernetes secret with client ID/secret/cookie_secret using services/rater_backend_v3/oauth/k8s-oauth2-proxy.yaml
+ - Ensure cert-manager is installed and ClusterIssuer (k8s/ingress/cert-manager-clusterissuer.yaml) configured
+ - Deploy oauth2-proxy and rater ingress (k8s/rater/rater-ingress.yaml)
+
+5) Evidence & audit logging
+ - Create evidence S3 bucket with Object Lock enabled and set EVIDENCE_BUCKET secret
+ - Deploy fluentd evidence daemonset (services/evidence_store/k8s_fluentd_s3.yaml)
+
+6) IRSA & least privilege
+ - Integrate terraform/irsa_mapping.tf fragments into your infra code
+ - Remove plaintext secrets after validating secret manager references with ops/terraform/replace_plaintext_secrets.sh
+
+7) Sim stress & SME gating
+ - Use ops/sim/run_stress_and_gate.sh (or run via CI) to produce sim_report.json and require SME label via SME gate
+
+8) Drift & auto-fallback
+ - Deploy ops/monitoring/drift/auto_fallback.py as a cronjob or controller pod; configure env vars (TARGET_DEPLOYMENT, FALLBACK_IMAGE)
+
+Security & SME signoffs are required for all above steps.
